["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalRefType/vulnerabilityExploitabilityAssessment", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "A reference to a Vulnerability Exploitability eXchange (VEX) statement which provides information on whether a product is impacted by a specific vulnerability in an included package and, if affected, whether there are actions recommended to remediate. See also [NTIA VEX one-page summary](https://ntia.gov/files/ntia/publications/vex_one-page_summary.pdf).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:N90f85bd0c7f947e1b67c3066c8123a25", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest", "_:N4967883a431c41f3bdd4a855261203eb", "localId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Security/CvssSeverityType/medium", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label", "medium", "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Security/SsvcDecisionType/attend", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "The vulnerability requires attention from the organization's internal, supervisory-level individuals. Necessary actions include requesting assistance or information about the vulnerability, and may involve publishing a notification either internally and/or externally. CISA recommends remediating Attend vulnerabilities sooner than standard update timelines.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:N8b3524279a2e4d99af17021171e662e6", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest", "_:N635a74d595db4b2ca133589e23db80f8", "localId", "", ""]
